TASK A1 – DESIGN THE POLYMORPHIC BILL HIERARCHY (7 Marks)
A1.1 – Identify the Common Interface (2 Marks)
Common data members:
- Patient name
- Bill ID
- Date of billing
Common operations:
- total() – calculates the total bill amount.
- type() – returns the type of bill.
- print() – displays bill details.
All bills share a common interface, but each bill calculates its total differently.
A1.2 – Design the Hierarchy (3 Marks)
Abstract Base Class: Bill
- Contains common data members such as patient name and bill ID.
- Contains pure virtual functions total() and type().
- Contains a virtual destructor.
- Derived classes override the virtual functions.
Derived classes:
1. OutPatientBill – consultation charges + test charges.
2. InPatientBill – room charges + procedure charges + medicine charges.
3. DayCareBill – fixed package charges.
4. EmergencyBill – base charges + time-based charges.
